{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 PDP — the VARIANT LEDGER MODEL (WINNING-SPEC §3.6 option-axis rule + §4.4 ledger).
  Built ONCE from product.variants, in Liquid, and printed in two shapes:

    A. a delimited text model the no-JS markup is built from   (emit: 'rows', the default)
    B. one <script type="application/json"> tag for the JS     (emit: 'json')

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ call signatures
    {%- capture env2_model -%}
      {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants', product: product, axis: section.settings.price_axis_option -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign env2_recs = env2_model | split: '~~R~~' -%}
    {%- assign env2_meta = env2_recs[0] | split: '~~F~~' -%}
    {%- for env2_rec in env2_recs offset: 1 -%}
      {%- assign r = env2_rec | split: '~~F~~' -%}   …r[10] is the price, r[15] the variant id…
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants', product: product, emit: 'json' -%}   (prints the script tag)

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ inputs
    product : required. Blank / no variants -> prints nothing at all.
    axis    : which option carries the price. 'option1' | 'option2' | 'option3' | 1 | 2 | 3.
              Blank / 0 -> DETECTED (see below). This is the section's price_axis_option setting.
    axis2   : a second price-bearing option (product C: עוצמה × גוון אור). Blank -> detected.
    emit    : 'rows' (default) | 'json'
    json_id : id of the script tag in json mode (default 'env2-pdp-variants')

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ axis detection (§3.6)
    1. If one option's value fully determines the price (every variant sharing that value has the same
       price) and it has more than one value, that option is the price axis. (A: אורך ומספר נורות.)
    2. Otherwise the first PAIR of options that together determine the price becomes the axis + axis2.
       (C: עוצמה × גוון אור -> four rows 219.90 / 222.90 / 249.90 / 252.90.)
    3. Otherwise (one price for the whole product) the option with the most values is the row axis.
    Every option that is not axis/axis2 is a "quiet" axis: it never changes the price, it is rendered
    as a <select name="id"> inside the row form (§4.4) and as a hairline radio line or a select in the
    stage (§3.6), and when it has ONE value it is not rendered as a control at all — meta[8] says how
    many values it has so the section can obey "no one-value picker".
    product.variants.size == 1  ->  meta[1] = 'single': there is no picker; the ledger is a QUANTITY
    ledger (§4.4 product B) posting quantity=N against meta[11].

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the number parse
    The row's leading option value is parsed for up to two numbers and their units, so the ledger can
    print "5 מ׳ · 20 נורות · 89.90 ₪ · ≈ 17.98 ₪ למטר" with nothing typed:
        "5 מ׳ / 20 נורות" -> n1 5 · u1 מ׳ · n2 20 · u2 נורות
        "2 יחידות"        -> n1 2 · u1 יחידות
        "6W"              -> n1 6 · u1 W
    per_unit is computed ONLY for a length or a count unit (מ׳ / מטר / יח׳ / יחידות / יחידה) — a
    price per watt is meaningless, so C's rows carry no per-unit figure. It is price ÷ n1 rounded to
    the agora (never a 1-decimal figure, §4.4).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ record layout   (fields ~~F~~, records ~~R~~)
    meta = records[0]
      0  'meta'
      1  mode                 'variants' | 'single'
      2  axis                 1-based option position carrying the price
      3  axis2                1-based, or 0
      4  axis_name            e.g. 'אורך ומספר נורות'
      5  axis2_name           '' when none
      6  quiet_axis           1-based position of the first non-price option, 0 when none
      7  quiet_name           e.g. 'צבע תאורה'
      8  quiet_values         how many values that quiet axis has  (1 -> never render a picker)
      9  rows                 number of row records that follow
      10 default_row          0-based index of the row holding selected_or_first_available_variant
      11 default_variant_id
      12 price_min            '89.90'
      13 price_max            '179.90'
      14 price_varies         '1' | '0'
      15 unit                 u1 of the first row ('מ׳' | 'יח׳' | 'W' | '')
      16 count_unit           u2 of the first row ('נורות' | '')
      17 per_unit_label       '₪ למטר' | '₪ ליחידה' | ''
      18 axis_values          how many values the price axis has (1 -> the ledger has a single row)
      19 'e'                  terminator — a trailing EMPTY field is dropped by split, so every record
                              ends with a literal 'e' and no real field is ever the last one
    row records (one per price step, in the option's own value order)
      0  'row'
      1  i                    0-based
      2  key                  the row's value(s), ' / ' joined  ("6W / אור חם 3000K")
      3  key_a                the axis value                    ("6W")
      4  key_b                the axis2 value, '' when none     ("אור חם 3000K")
      5  label                = key (kept separate so a section may relabel without losing the key)
      6  n1                   '5'   ''
      7  u1                   'מ׳'  ''
      8  n2                   '20'  ''
      9  u2                   'נורות' ''
      10 price                '89.90'     (the row's lowest price; a row never spans two prices)
      11 price_cents          '8990'
      12 per_unit             '17.98' or ''
      13 per_unit_label       '₪ למטר' | '₪ ליחידה' | ''
      14 available            '1' | '0'
      15 variant_id           the first AVAILABLE variant of the row (else the first)
      16 variant_count
      17 quiet                'id^label^price_cents^avail;id^label^price_cents^avail'  (';' separated,
                              no trailing separator) — the row's <select name="id"> options, in variant order
      18 image                variant image url (1200) or '' — C has one on 5 of 8 variants (§3.5)
      19 'e'                  terminator (see meta[19])
    Nothing here is escaped: escape at the point of use ({{ r[2] | escape }}), exactly as the rest of
    the theme does. The JSON emit escapes with the json filter.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_ok = false
  if product != blank and product.variants.size > 0
    assign env2_ok = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if env2_ok -%}
{%- liquid
  assign FS = '~~F~~'
  assign RS = '~~R~~'
  assign nopt = product.options_with_values.size

  # 0. explicit axis parameters ('option2' and 2 both work)
  assign ax = axis | default: 0 | remove: 'option' | plus: 0
  assign ax2 = axis2 | default: 0 | remove: 'option' | plus: 0
  if ax > nopt
    assign ax = 0
  endif
  if ax2 > nopt or ax2 == ax
    assign ax2 = 0
  endif

  # 1. how many distinct prices does this product have at all
  assign pset = '|'
  for v in product.variants
    assign pk = '|' | append: v.price | append: '|'
    unless pset contains pk
      assign pset = pset | append: v.price | append: '|'
    endunless
  endfor
  assign nprice = pset | split: '|' | size | minus: 1

  # 2. does ONE option determine the price
  if ax == 0 and nprice > 1
    for opt in product.options_with_values
      assign oi = forloop.index
      assign oi0 = forloop.index0
      if ax == 0 and opt.values.size > 1
        assign map = '|'
        assign consistent = true
        for v in product.variants
          assign val = v.options[oi0] | replace: '|', '¦' | replace: '=', '≡'
          assign kk = '|' | append: val | append: '='
          assign parts = map | split: kk
          if parts.size > 1
            assign prev = parts[1] | split: '|' | first
            assign cur = v.price | append: ''
            unless prev == cur
              assign consistent = false
            endunless
          else
            assign map = map | append: val | append: '=' | append: v.price | append: '|'
          endif
        endfor
        if consistent
          assign ax = oi
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  # 3. otherwise, does a PAIR of options determine it (product C)
  if ax == 0 and nprice > 1 and nopt > 1
    for oa in product.options_with_values
      assign ia = forloop.index
      assign ia0 = forloop.index0
      for ob in product.options_with_values
        assign ib = forloop.index
        assign ib0 = forloop.index0
        if ax == 0 and ib > ia
          assign map = '|'
          assign consistent = true
          for v in product.variants
            assign val = v.options[ia0] | append: '§' | append: v.options[ib0] | replace: '|', '¦' | replace: '=', '≡'
            assign kk = '|' | append: val | append: '='
            assign parts = map | split: kk
            if parts.size > 1
              assign prev = parts[1] | split: '|' | first
              assign cur = v.price | append: ''
              unless prev == cur
                assign consistent = false
              endunless
            else
              assign map = map | append: val | append: '=' | append: v.price | append: '|'
            endif
          endfor
          if consistent
            assign ax = ia
            assign ax2 = ib
          endif
        endif
      endfor
    endfor
  endif

  # 4. one price for the whole product (or nothing detected): the widest option is the row axis
  if ax == 0
    assign widest = 0
    for opt in product.options_with_values
      if opt.values.size > widest
        assign widest = opt.values.size
        assign ax = forloop.index
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if ax == 0
    assign ax = 1
  endif

  assign ax0 = ax | minus: 1
  assign optA = product.options_with_values[ax0]
  assign ax20 = 0
  if ax2 > 0
    assign ax20 = ax2 | minus: 1
    assign optB = product.options_with_values[ax20]
  endif

  # 5. the quiet axis: the first option that does not carry the price
  assign qax = 0
  assign qname = ''
  assign qvals = 0
  for opt in product.options_with_values
    if qax == 0 and forloop.index != ax and forloop.index != ax2
      assign qax = forloop.index
      assign qname = opt.name
      assign qvals = opt.values.size
    endif
  endfor

  # 6. the row keys, in the option's own value order, only those that exist as variants
  assign keys = ''
  for va in optA.values
    if ax2 > 0
      for vb in optB.values
        assign combo = va | append: '§' | append: vb
        assign present = false
        for v in product.variants
          assign c2 = v.options[ax0] | append: '§' | append: v.options[ax20]
          if c2 == combo
            assign present = true
          endif
        endfor
        if present
          assign keys = keys | append: combo | append: '¤'
        endif
      endfor
    else
      assign present = false
      for v in product.variants
        if v.options[ax0] == va
          assign present = true
        endif
      endfor
      if present
        assign keys = keys | append: va | append: '¤'
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  assign rowkeys = keys | split: '¤'
  # Ruby's split drops a trailing empty field and python's does not — count and skip explicitly so the
  # model is identical on both engines.
  assign nrows = 0
  for rk in rowkeys
    unless rk == blank
      assign nrows = nrows | plus: 1
    endunless
  endfor

  # 7. the rows
  assign sel = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first
  if ax2 > 0
    assign selkey = sel.options[ax0] | append: '§' | append: sel.options[ax20]
  else
    assign selkey = sel.options[ax0]
  endif
  assign defrow = 0
  assign meta_unit = ''
  assign meta_cunit = ''
  assign meta_perlabel = ''
  assign body = ''

  assign ri = -1
  for rk in rowkeys
    if rk == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign ri = ri | plus: 1
    if rk == selkey
      assign defrow = ri
    endif
    assign kparts = rk | split: '§'
    assign key_a = kparts[0]
    assign key_b = ''
    if kparts.size > 1
      assign key_b = kparts[1]
    endif
    assign label = kparts | join: ' / '

    # 7a. aggregate the variants of this row
    assign rprice = 0
    assign rid = 0
    assign ravail = false
    assign rn = 0
    assign quiet = ''
    assign rimg = ''
    for v in product.variants
      if ax2 > 0
        assign c2 = v.options[ax0] | append: '§' | append: v.options[ax20]
      else
        assign c2 = v.options[ax0]
      endif
      if c2 == rk
        assign rn = rn | plus: 1
        if rprice == 0 or v.price < rprice
          assign rprice = v.price
        endif
        if rid == 0
          assign rid = v.id
        endif
        if v.available and ravail == false
          assign ravail = true
          assign rid = v.id
        endif
        assign ql = ''
        for ov in v.options
          assign ovi = forloop.index
          unless ovi == ax or ovi == ax2
            if ql == ''
              assign ql = ov
            else
              assign ql = ql | append: ' · ' | append: ov
            endif
          endunless
        endfor
        assign qa = '0'
        if v.available
          assign qa = '1'
        endif
        if quiet != ''
          assign quiet = quiet | append: ';'
        endif
        assign quiet = quiet | append: v.id | append: '^' | append: ql | append: '^' | append: v.price | append: '^' | append: qa
        if rimg == '' and v.image != blank
          assign rimg = v.image | image_url: width: 1200
        endif
      endif
    endfor

    # 7b. parse up to two numbers + units out of the axis value
    assign n1 = ''
    assign u1 = ''
    assign n2 = ''
    assign u2 = ''
    assign toks = key_a | split: ' '
    for t in toks
      assign numpart = ''
      assign rest = ''
      assign stopped = false
      assign chars = t | split: ''
      for ch in chars
        if stopped
          assign rest = rest | append: ch
        else
          if '0123456789.' contains ch
            assign numpart = numpart | append: ch
          else
            assign stopped = true
            assign rest = rest | append: ch
          endif
        endif
      endfor
      if numpart != ''
        if n1 == ''
          assign n1 = numpart
          assign u1 = rest
        elsif n2 == ''
          assign n2 = numpart
          assign u2 = rest
        endif
      else
        if n1 != '' and u1 == '' and n2 == '' and rest != '/' and rest != '·' and rest != '-'
          assign u1 = rest
        elsif n2 != '' and u2 == '' and rest != '/' and rest != '·' and rest != '-'
          assign u2 = rest
        endif
      endif
    endfor

    # 7c. per-unit price, only for a length or a count
    assign per = ''
    assign perlabel = ''
    if n1 != ''
      assign nnum = n1 | plus: 0.0
      if nnum > 0
        if u1 == 'מ׳' or u1 == 'מ' or u1 == 'מטר' or u1 == 'מטרים'
          assign per = rprice | divided_by: nnum | round | money_without_currency
          assign perlabel = '₪ למטר'
        elsif u1 == 'יח׳' or u1 == 'יח' or u1 == 'יחידה' or u1 == 'יחידות'
          assign per = rprice | divided_by: nnum | round | money_without_currency
          assign perlabel = '₪ ליחידה'
        endif
      endif
    endif
    if ri == 0
      assign meta_unit = u1
      assign meta_cunit = u2
      assign meta_perlabel = perlabel
    endif

    assign av = '0'
    if ravail
      assign av = '1'
    endif
    assign rprice_txt = rprice | money_without_currency
    assign rec = 'row' | append: FS | append: ri | append: FS | append: label | append: FS | append: key_a | append: FS | append: key_b | append: FS | append: label | append: FS | append: n1 | append: FS | append: u1 | append: FS | append: n2 | append: FS | append: u2 | append: FS
    assign rec = rec | append: rprice_txt | append: FS | append: rprice | append: FS | append: per | append: FS | append: perlabel | append: FS | append: av | append: FS | append: rid | append: FS | append: rn | append: FS | append: quiet | append: FS | append: rimg | append: FS | append: 'e'
    assign body = body | append: RS | append: rec
  endfor

  # 8. the meta record
  assign mode = 'variants'
  if product.variants.size == 1
    assign mode = 'single'
  endif
  assign varies = '0'
  if product.price_varies
    assign varies = '1'
  endif
  assign ax2name = ''
  if ax2 > 0
    assign ax2name = optB.name
  endif
  assign pmin_txt = product.price_min | money_without_currency
  assign pmax_txt = product.price_max | money_without_currency
  assign meta = 'meta' | append: FS | append: mode | append: FS | append: ax | append: FS | append: ax2 | append: FS | append: optA.name | append: FS | append: ax2name | append: FS | append: qax | append: FS | append: qname | append: FS | append: qvals | append: FS | append: nrows | append: FS | append: defrow | append: FS | append: sel.id | append: FS
  assign meta = meta | append: pmin_txt | append: FS | append: pmax_txt | append: FS | append: varies | append: FS | append: meta_unit | append: FS | append: meta_cunit | append: FS | append: meta_perlabel | append: FS | append: optA.values.size | append: FS | append: 'e'
  assign env2_model = meta | append: body
-%}
{%- assign env2_emit = emit | default: 'rows' -%}
{%- if env2_emit == 'json' -%}
{%- liquid
  assign recs = env2_model | split: RS
  assign m = recs[0] | split: FS
-%}
<script type="application/json" id="{{ json_id | default: 'env2-pdp-variants' }}" data-env2-pdp-variants>{ "mode": {{ m[1] | json }}, "axis": {{ m[2] | plus: 0 }}, "axis2": {{ m[3] | plus: 0 }}, "axisName": {{ m[4] | json }}, "axis2Name": {{ m[5] | json }}, "quietAxis": {{ m[6] | plus: 0 }}, "quietName": {{ m[7] | json }}, "quietValues": {{ m[8] | plus: 0 }}, "rowCount": {{ m[9] | plus: 0 }}, "defaultRow": {{ m[10] | plus: 0 }}, "defaultId": {{ m[11] | plus: 0 }}, "priceMin": {{ m[12] | json }}, "priceMax": {{ m[13] | json }}, "priceVaries": {% if m[14] == '1' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}, "unit": {{ m[15] | json }}, "countUnit": {{ m[16] | json }}, "perUnitLabel": {{ m[17] | json }}, "axisValues": {{ m[18] | plus: 0 }}, "rows": [{% for rec in recs offset: 1 %}{%- assign r = rec | split: FS -%}{% unless forloop.first %}, {% endunless %}{ "i": {{ r[1] | plus: 0 }}, "key": {{ r[2] | json }}, "a": {{ r[3] | json }}, "b": {{ r[4] | json }}, "label": {{ r[5] | json }}, "n1": {{ r[6] | json }}, "u1": {{ r[7] | json }}, "n2": {{ r[8] | json }}, "u2": {{ r[9] | json }}, "priceText": {{ r[10] | json }}, "price": {{ r[11] | plus: 0 }}, "perUnit": {{ r[12] | json }}, "perUnitLabel": {{ r[13] | json }}, "available": {% if r[14] == '1' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}, "id": {{ r[15] | plus: 0 }}, "variantCount": {{ r[16] | plus: 0 }}, "image": {{ r[18] | json }}, "variants": [{% assign qs = r[17] | split: ';' %}{% for q in qs %}{%- assign qf = q | split: '^' -%}{% unless forloop.first %}, {% endunless %}{ "id": {{ qf[0] | plus: 0 }}, "label": {{ qf[1] | json }}, "price": {{ qf[2] | plus: 0 }}, "available": {% if qf[3] == '1' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %} }{% endfor %}] }{% endfor %}] }</script>
{%- else -%}
{{- env2_model -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
